; Message carries a typed request to Flow for one metaflow.
; Flow resolves Up relative to the sending metaflow, holds the queue,
; and applies its wake rule. Message records no messages or ids.
; Send identifies its socket peer through process ancestry.
; SendThread additionally carries the harness-stamped native thread id.
; Neither request carries a PID or sender address. Message reads its peer
; from the kernel and Flow verifies the configured MCP/app-server pair.
; Configure sets the ordinary, Meta and Flow socket paths. An ordinary
; Configure is refused after Meta Configure has been accepted.

Signal
[ signal_flow:[ Address Recipient Request Process Lock NativeSessionId
  SendPayloadSize ActualBytes MaximumBytes ]
  message_library:Configuration ]
[ Send.{ Recipient Request }
  Configure.Configuration
  SendThread.{ Recipient Request NativeSessionId } ]
[ Delivered
  Woken
  Queued
  Configured
  Refused.SendRefusal ]
[ SendRefusal.[ Unidentified.Process
  Unknown.[ Address.Address Lock.Lock ]
  Ended.Address
  Asleep
  NoneAbove
  OffRoute
  Held.Lock
  Locked
  Lapsed
  NotMessage
  NoLayer
  Store.String
  FlowUnreachable
  AlreadyConfigured
  NotConfigured
  NotSendServer.Process
  Oversized.SendPayloadSize ] ]
